TESTDATA["pet8-t3"] = {"title":"Cambridge PET 8 · Test 3","format":"2010","reading":[{"part":1,"items":[{"n":1,"text":"Karen,\nYour French teacher rang earlier – the Tuesday evening class you wanted next term is full, but Thursday's available if you can go then instead. He'll ring back later.\nJan","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["Karen has the possibility of attending French classes on two evenings per week.","Karen's evening classes will now start at an earlier time this term.","Karen needs to decide whether to change the evening that she has classes."],"answer":"C"},{"n":2,"text":"LOCAL FARMERS SUPPLY ALL THIS SUPERMARKET'S VEGETABLES – KEEPING PRICES LOW FOR OUR CUSTOMERS!","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["We get fresh vegetables from the farmers with the cheapest prices.","We promise you won't find lower-priced fresh food than ours.","We buy our fresh vegetables locally to save you money."],"answer":"C"},{"n":3,"text":"Jack,\nMy car broke down on the motorway, so I'll be late picking you up. I'm on the way again now – see you at your house in 30 minutes.\nDavid","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["David is fixing his broken car on the motorway at the moment.","David is half an hour away from where Jack lives.","David is hoping Jack will collect him in his car soon."],"answer":"B"},{"n":4,"text":"To: Denise\nFrom: Maria\nAbout that sweater you borrowed for skiing last time – could you bring it round to my place? I'm going snowboarding with Mark soon and it'll be cold!","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["Maria needs Denise to return something she lent her a while ago.","Maria is inviting Denise to go somewhere with her and Mark.","Maria wants to borrow something from Denise that she can wear for snowboarding."],"answer":"A"},{"n":5,"text":"PARKING\nHOSPITAL VISITORS ONLY\nWAITING LIMITED TO TWO HOURS\nFOLLOW SIGNS TO STAFF PARKING","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["Only hospital visitors can park here for longer than two hours.","Members of hospital staff are allowed to leave their cars here.","This car park is for people visiting the hospital for a short time."],"answer":"C"}]},{"part":2,"people":[{"n":6,"name":"Victor and Olga","text":"Victor and Olga need a personal instructor to teach them better powerboat skills, and to find their way safely around the waters off the coast. They want to go without booking in advance.","answer":"D"},{"n":7,"name":"Felipe","text":"Felipe wants a weekend training session for his staff, to help them work well together. He'd like them to do sailing and indoor activities, and have comfortable overnight accommodation at the centre.","answer":"H"},{"n":8,"name":"Harry","text":"Harry wants to find a centre where top people in watersports train and where he can measure his skills to see if he could compete professionally. However, he can't afford anything too expensive.","answer":"E"},{"n":9,"name":"Tania and Paolo","text":"Tania and Paolo can already waterski, and want to try another challenging watersport. They want to go in the evenings, and be able to eat at the centre afterwards.","answer":"B"},{"n":10,"name":"Laura and Adam","text":"Laura and Adam want to celebrate Laura's birthday at a watersports centre with friends, some of whom prefer to do indoor sports. They'd like to have a good idea of what the place is like before going.","answer":"F"}],"texts":[{"letter":"A","title":"Fossey Centre","text":"The Fossey Centre has indoor and outdoor activities. Anyone wanting a high lake with watersports facilities good enough for even professionals to practise on, plus indoor football and tennis. No individual training is available. However, there's no need to book in advance as the Centre is rarely busy."},{"letter":"B","title":"Marinewater","text":"The Marinewater website shows their whole range of watersports from sailing to the exciting experience of controlling a boat on a fast-moving river. The route is used by professional athletes in training, so it is lit until late, while the Centre's restaurant serves delicious meals. Booking is recommended."},{"letter":"C","title":"Blore Centre","text":"If you're looking for somewhere to provide staff training, then the Blore Centre is perfect. There's a range of activities, with powerboats, sailing or an indoor sports centre – ideal for team-building. There's accommodation for overnight stays but it's extremely basic."},{"letter":"D","title":"Marston Centre","text":"The Marston Centre offers courses at all levels for learning to manage every kind of boat you can think of. Fees for private teaching sessions are reasonable, and it isn't essential to arrange this before you go. The centre also offers training in how not to get lost at sea. See their website!"},{"letter":"E","title":"Padcaster Centre","text":"The huge lake at the Padcaster Centre is perfect for waterskiing and sailing. It's regularly used by sportspeople preparing for the Olympics, and has a cycle path around the outside for your coach to accompany you on land and check your speed. See how you compare with the champions! Prices are very fair."},{"letter":"F","title":"Camford Centre","text":"The Camford Centre offers sailing for people who love relaxing on the water, and also has volleyball and badminton courts in its well-designed building. Check out their website – their 360-degree video tours show you exactly what's available. And if you're coming for a special occasion, tell us – we'll prepare a fantastic meal in our restaurant."},{"letter":"G","title":"Casson Centre","text":"The Casson Centre and café are open all day until 9 pm. The Centre's professional staff offer individual training in sailing and waterskiing, for which booking is required. The small hotel on site is useful for anyone travelling a long way to the Centre."},{"letter":"H","title":"Aqua Sports","text":"Aqua Sports offers company team-building courses that can include water sports on the lake or a range of things to do in the gym. You can select the perfect timetable for your team. Afterwards, you can have a good night's sleep in the Centre's excellent hotel."}]},{"part":3,"title":"My first long motorbiking trip – by Graham Jones","text":"I began riding motorbikes when I was eighteen years old, as a passenger on the back of my friend Luke's bike. It was a classic motorbike – big, fast, and noisy! Our first few rides were short trips – which he was very careful to make as enjoyable as possible for me – and as a result I fell in love with the whole motorbike experience almost immediately.\n\nAfter a couple of months of shorter rides, we went on a longer group ride with Luke's motorcycling club, which he said would give me a good idea of the pleasures and difficulties of motorcycling. We rode approximately 100 km in one day, and it was a great experience – although we only managed to get less than half of the way to our destination. The ride was wonderful and we had beautiful weather as we went along the quiet roads. However, after we'd stopped to have lunch, one rider in the group, Tania, suddenly found her bike wouldn't start. Some people in the group finally managed to get it going, but in the end Tania had to turn round and go back home by herself, knowing that if she stopped anywhere, she wouldn't be able to start her bike again. She bravely decided she could ride back home alone, but I doubted whether I'd have such a confident attitude in the same situation.\n\nOur group then drove on to the mountains and stopped for some lunch – and that's where things started to go wrong. The weather turned bad and it began to snow. Then, without asking anyone, the leader of the group had the idea of going in a completely new direction up a steep mountain road, with corners that would be difficult for motorbikes even when the weather was good – and by now it was snowing quite heavily.\n\nWhen we finally made it to the top of the mountain, Luke was annoyed. He said it was too risky to be on a mountain in such bad weather, and that we should go back down. We were both frozen when we reached the bottom, despite our cold-weather clothes. However, when we got back to my house we both began to see the funny side of it all, and I immediately asked Luke when we could go again. I realised I could cope with the worst of times on a motorbike, and there and then I made up my mind to try and save up for one.","items":[{"n":11,"q":"Graham says his friend Luke was keen for him to enjoy riding motorbikes.","answer":"A"},{"n":12,"q":"Luke was confident their first ride with his club would be a totally positive experience.","answer":"B"},{"n":13,"q":"For Graham's first group ride, they planned to go to a place 100 kilometres away.","answer":"B"},{"n":14,"q":"One rider in their group, Tania, started her bike without help when it broke down.","answer":"B"},{"n":15,"q":"Graham wondered if he would feel the same as Tania if his bike had the same problem.","answer":"A"},{"n":16,"q":"At one point, the group leader decided to change the route they were following.","answer":"A"},{"n":17,"q":"Luke was concerned that the weather conditions were making their ride dangerous.","answer":"A"},{"n":18,"q":"They found that the clothes they were wearing protected them from the weather.","answer":"B"},{"n":19,"q":"Luke and Graham's mood improved after they reached Graham's house.","answer":"A"},{"n":20,"q":"Immediately after the trip Graham bought a new motorbike of his own.","answer":"B"}]},{"part":4,"title":"American Black Ducks","text":"I work at a US university where my team and I are trying to learn more about water birds, particularly one called the American black duck. And we've just started using an exciting piece of equipment called a 'night-vision scope', which allows us to see the ducks in the dark!\n\nWe're worried about black ducks mainly because their numbers have fallen hugely and we don't know whether there's enough food on the east coast for them during winter. There's lots of information about their daytime activities, but nothing about what they do at night, because we simply haven't had the equipment. But this new 'scope' will produce really clear pictures, even on moonless nights, so we'll be able to find out more and make better decisions about looking after the area where they live based on what we learn.\n\nIt is very hard work. There are four of us, each working six hours daily. We've studied ducks in different locations, and I've had to take a boat to some sites and make notes on every duck I see. The weather hasn't helped – some nights are mild, but more often it's wet. Oh, and it's a quiet job – and needs lots of coffee to stop me falling asleep! We've only missed one working day so far, because the snow was too deep even for our special snow vehicles.\n\nStill I like the challenge of it, especially compared to what the summer will bring – hours in a laboratory, where we'll look at our results together. It'll be hard to be stuck inside – but it's essential to do this. And I wouldn't change it for anything!","items":[{"n":21,"q":"What is Sam Prentice doing in the text?","options":["describing how he became a wildlife biologist","explaining how he is doing a piece of research","suggesting how readers can learn about one type of bird","giving a report of success he's had in his work"],"answer":"B"},{"n":22,"q":"What is Sam hoping to discover about American black ducks?","options":["what their behaviour is like after dark","which kind of food they need to live on","which animals are responsible for the fall in their numbers","what makes the east coast a suitable location for them"],"answer":"A"},{"n":23,"q":"When Sam spends long periods watching ducks, he","options":["dislikes having to deal with low temperatures.","finds there's enough to do to maintain his interest.","is glad of the chance to be in a quiet place.","sometimes finds it difficult to stay awake."],"answer":"D"},{"n":24,"q":"What does Sam say about working inside a lab over the summer?","options":["He feels pleased that he'll avoid the hot weather.","He accepts that it's a necessary part of his job.","He's looking forward to studying his results.","He's glad he'll be working with other people."],"answer":"B"},{"n":25,"q":"What might Sam say about his experiences of working outdoors?","options":["Having the right vehicle for bad weather has meant we've still carried on working, whatever it's been like outside.","We decided that we'd only go to sites that were easy to get to, and I'm really glad we made that decision.","Sometimes the moon hasn't been very bright, but our equipment provides the amount of light we need to collect information.","The other people in my team are brilliant, but it's been hard watching ducks in the same place every day."],"answer":"C"}]},{"part":5,"title":"Wool","text":"Wool comes from sheep and (0) ……… (certain) other animals like goats and rabbits. Over a million tonnes of wool is produced every year, of [26] 60% goes into clothes. The wool that is used [27] comes from Australian Merino sheep. Their wool is good for baby clothes, as it is soft, [28] babies warm, and can [29] their bodies.\n\nWhen wool is first cut from the sheep, it [30] a high level of valuable oil, so before the wool is used, it must be cleaned. The [31] way to do this is by putting the wool in warm water. The oil that is [32] from the wool is widely used in products like hand creams.\n\nSheep were first used by humans several thousand years ago, [33] it is believed that this was for meat [34] than wool. When people developed a way of cutting the wool from sheep it [35] a more important material.","gaps":{"26":{"options":["what","whose","which","that"],"answer":"C"},"27":{"options":["mostly","nearly","properly","truly"],"answer":"A"},"28":{"options":["stays","helps","rests","keeps"],"answer":"D"},"29":{"options":["protect","wrap","care","save"],"answer":"A"},"30":{"options":["involves","contains","receives","consists"],"answer":"B"},"31":{"options":["simplest","clearest","plainest","nearest"],"answer":"A"},"32":{"options":["carried","passed","removed","divided"],"answer":"C"},"33":{"options":["while","but","or","because"],"answer":"B"},"34":{"options":["rather","instead","apart","except"],"answer":"A"},"35":{"options":["arrived","turned","grew","became"],"answer":"D"}}}],"writing":[{"part":1,"title":"Here are some sentences about buying a sports car.","items":[{"n":1,"first":"His friend Frieda suggested that Ben should buy a second-hand car.","before":"'Why","after":"a second-hand car, Ben?' suggested Frieda.","answers":["not buy","don't you buy","do you not buy"]},{"n":2,"first":"Ben didn't have enough money for a new car.","before":"Ben couldn't afford","after":"buy a new car.","answers":["to"]},{"n":3,"first":"Ben contacted the owner of a car for sale after seeing an advert.","before":"Ben got in touch","after":"the owner of a car for sale after seeing an advert.","answers":["with"]},{"n":4,"first":"Ben drove the car and decided immediately that he liked it.","before":"Ben decided he liked the car as","after":"he drove it.","answers":["soon as"]},{"n":5,"first":"The car was cheaper than Ben had expected.","before":"The car was","after":"expensive than Ben had expected.","answers":["less"]}]},{"part":2,"items":[{"n":6,"kind":"message","task":"Your English friend, Alex, is coming to your town for the day, and wants to meet you.\n\nWrite an email to Alex. In your email, you should\n• explain where you can meet\n• suggest what you can do together\n• advise Alex what to bring.\n\nWrite 35–45 words on your answer sheet.","points":["spiegare dove potete incontrarvi","suggerire che cosa potete fare insieme","consigliare ad Alex che cosa portare"]}]},{"part":3,"items":[{"n":7,"kind":"letter","task":"This is part of a letter you receive from an English friend.\n\n'I've won some prize money in a competition, and I'm not sure what to do. My family think I should save the money, but I want to spend it all on an exciting holiday. What should I do?'\n\nNow write a letter to your friend, giving your advice.\nWrite your letter in about 100 words on your answer sheet."},{"n":8,"kind":"story","task":"Your English teacher wants you to write a story.\nThis is the title for your story:\n\nThe day I met my hero\n\nWrite your story in about 100 words on your answer sheet."}]}],"listening":[{"part":1,"audio":"audio/pet8-t3-l1.mp3","items":[{"n":1,"q":"How are they going to get to the café?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"A"},{"n":2,"q":"What has the man had a problem with?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"},{"n":3,"q":"When does the man plan to get up?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"B"},{"n":4,"q":"What are they going to order?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"},{"n":5,"q":"What is the woman phoning about?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"A"},{"n":6,"q":"What are they going to watch first?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"},{"n":7,"q":"What is the woman going to buy?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"}],"example":"img/pet8-t3-l1-ex.jpg"},{"part":2,"intro":"You will hear an interview with a young man called Jack Salter, who has won a photography competition.","audio":"audio/pet8-t3-l2.mp3","items":[{"n":8,"q":"Why did Jack take photographs of street signs?","options":["His mother suggested it.","The colours were exciting.","He liked their different shapes."],"answer":"B"},{"n":9,"q":"Why did Jack go into his yard to take his winning photo?","options":["He wanted to be out in the sunshine.","He was looking for shots of flowers.","He was trying out some new equipment."],"answer":"C"},{"n":10,"q":"When Jack first looked at his winning photo, he felt","options":["proud of how good it was.","worried about the background.","unsure how clear the detail was."],"answer":"C"},{"n":11,"q":"Jack was surprised by the other photos in the competition because","options":["the quality was so high.","the styles were so similar.","the subjects were so unusual."],"answer":"A"},{"n":12,"q":"Since winning the competition, Jack now hopes to","options":["take more photos of people.","travel to different countries.","get ideas from other photographers."],"answer":"B"},{"n":13,"q":"Jack advises other young people interested in photography to","options":["have the same attitude as him.","photograph the same things as him.","get the same type of camera as him."],"answer":"A"}]},{"part":3,"intro":"You will hear some information about a student running club.","audio":"audio/pet8-t3-l3.mp3","notes":"STUDENT RUNNING CLUB\nThe club meets at the [14] in the town.\nLast year's members will be sent a registration form by [15].\nMembers who pay $5 receive a special [16] that shows the club's name.\nAll runners will get a [17] as a free gift.\nYou know the runner's level of experience by the colour of their [18].\nContact Caryl [19] on 8302195.","answers":{"14":["football stadium","the football stadium"],"15":["email","e-mail","an email"],"16":["sports bag","a sports bag","sport bag"],"17":["water bottle","a water bottle","bottle of water"],"18":["shirt","shirts","a shirt"],"19":["BEATON","Beaton"]}},{"part":4,"intro":"You will hear a woman called Anne and a man called Peter talking about a college party.","audio":"audio/pet8-t3-l4.mp3","items":[{"n":20,"q":"Peter wants to take his sister to the party.","answer":"B"},{"n":21,"q":"Anne hopes the party will be bigger than the one last year.","answer":"B"},{"n":22,"q":"Peter thinks the new college hall is big enough for the party.","answer":"A"},{"n":23,"q":"Peter thinks DJs play a good range of music.","answer":"B"},{"n":24,"q":"Anne hopes the college cafeteria will supply the food for the party.","answer":"B"},{"n":25,"q":"Peter is confident the party will end after midnight.","answer":"A"}]}]};
